MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The flap discs felt like a natural follow-up to my cutting wheels because smoothing edges is a useful next step after cutting metal, provided they fit my grinder.",
    "The small stainless screws fit my repeated interest in fastening and assembly supplies. Gloves and cut-to-size foam also support practical tasks around adhesive work and cushioning parts, subject to suitable protection and dimensions."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Neither PLA filament nor printer resin fits an established need: I have not shown that I own a 3D printer, and tabletop epoxy serves a different purpose from UV-curing printer resin.",
    "Foam-gun cleaner needs a specific tool I have not shown I use. The brass rods and emergency switch likewise require particular projects that my general repair and fastening purchases do not establish."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in DIY supplies seems to have been stretched into an assumption that any specialized making material would be useful to me.",
    "Shared words such as resin and adhesive seem to carry too much weight when the products require different equipment or serve different tasks."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of screws, rivets, nuts, bolts and installation tools make practical fastening and assembly a stronger clue than a broad interest in making things.",
    "A useful recommendation needs to fit my tools, dimensions and current task. General workshop usefulness alone does not establish a need for a particular material or component."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my hands-on assembly work but extended it too far into specialized supplies without evidence of the equipment or projects they require."
}
